# 🎛️ FLAC_AX & AX AV Studio — Complete User Guide & Build Manual

---

## 🚀 1. Introduction: Why FLAC_AX Exists & How It Stacks Up

Modern desktop operating systems treat audio as a background convenience service. Even on purpose-built workstations, general-purpose audio stacks route sound through software mixers, sample-rate converters, dynamic thread schedulers, and power-managed USB hubs—introducing jitter, buffer underruns, and silent bit-depth truncation. Meanwhile, commercial audiophile players and standalone hardware synthesizers force a binary choice: either pay ongoing subscription fees for heavy desktop apps tethered to bloated operating systems, or spend thousands of dollars on dedicated proprietary DSP boxes with closed firmware and modest embedded CPUs.

**FLAC_AX** (`flac_ax` + `ax_av_studio`) rejects both compromises. Built in zero-dependency C++20 around a deterministic **`2:3:1` physical CPU core topology** on `Linux 6.12-rt` (`Piccolo [AX]`) and standard `x86_64` Linux workstations, it turns proven, off-the-shelf `x86_64` silicon (such as an Intel Core `i5-9600K` or `i5-8600K`) paired with an **ESS Sabre USB DAC** (HiBy FC3 / ES9281AC Pro) and **Akai MPK Mini MK3** into a deterministic, bare-metal audiophile transport and sub-millisecond live synthesizer workstation.

### ✨ What Makes FLAC_AX Special

1. **⚡ Deterministic `2:3:1` Core Partitioning (Zero Scheduler Contention)**
   Instead of letting the OS kernel migrate audio threads across cores alongside UI rendering and disk I/O, `FLAC_AX` pins workloads strictly by role:
   * **Cores `0–1` (System & UI Plane):** SDL2/OpenGL oscilloscope & 64-band FFT spectrum visualizer (`ax_av_studio`), off-RT MIDI OLED SysEx feedback, and OS housekeeping.
   * **Cores `2–4` (Real-Time DSP & Audio Plane):** `SCHED_FIFO` real-time audio callback and AVX2/SVF/reverb/delay synthesis—completely isolated from disk reads, heap allocations, and mutexes.
   * **Core `5` (I/O & Peripheral Plane):** Whole-album RAM preloading (`RamFilePreloader`), FLAC/DSD decoding, and lock-free ALSA RawMIDI ingestion (`MpkMini3Listener`).

2. **🧠 True RAM-Resident, Zero-Allocation Playback & Synthesis**
   * **`flac_ax` (Bit-Perfect Transport):** Preloads entire FLAC albums and native `.dsf`/`.dff` DSD64/DSD128 tracks into locked RAM on Core 5 before streaming raw `S32_LE` frames directly to `hw:CARD=FC3,DEV=0`—eliminating storage bus interrupts, PipeWire/PulseAudio resampling, and software volume scaling.
   * **`ax_av_studio` (Live AV Synthesizer):** Runs a 16-voice polyphonic melodic synth, 8-voice drum engine, 2-pole stereo State-Variable Filter, 4-comb `StereoReverbDsp`, and interpolated `TapeDelayDsp` entirely over preallocated `std::array` buffers with zero heap allocations on the real-time thread.

3. **🔒 Hardware-Level DAC Arbitration & USB Isochronous Tuning**
   Both binaries coordinate exclusive ownership of the ESS Sabre DAC via `/run/lock/ax-dac.lock` (`flock`), preventing accidental sample-rate collisions or device contention while automatically tuning `snd-usb-audio` (`nrpacks=1`) and disabling USB autosuspend for `VID 0x32BB`.

