## 🏗️ 2. System Architecture & `2:3:1` Topology

Both executables share the same deterministic hardware execution model so audio rendering never competes with disk decoding, MIDI polling, or OpenGL visualization:

* **🖥️ Cores `0–1` (System & UI Plane):**
  * `ax_av_studio`: Runs the SDL2/OpenGL 60 FPS oscilloscope and 64-band logarithmic FFT spectrum visualizer, drains the MIDI queue for HUD telemetry, and flushes rate-limited OLED feedback (`MpkMini3OledFeedback`) every `45 ms`.
  * `flac_ax`: Handles CLI control, terminal status reporting, and signal handling (`SIGINT`/`SIGTERM`).
* **⚡ Cores `2–4` (Real-Time Audio & DSP Plane):**
  * Runs the ALSA PCM playback loop (`SCHED_FIFO` priority) writing interleaved 32-bit signed (`S32_LE`) frames directly to `hw:CARD=FC3,DEV=0` with zero dynamic memory allocations, zero mutex locks, and zero file I/O.
* **🔌 Core `5` (Peripheral & Preload I/O Plane):**
  * `flac_ax`: Runs `PersistentDecoderWorker`, preloading entire FLAC albums or `.dsf`/`.dff` DSD64/DSD128 files into RAM (`RamFilePreloader`) and feeding the lock-free SPSC ring buffer.
  * `ax_av_studio`: Runs `MpkMini3Listener` (`ALSA RawMIDI` non-blocking reader) parsing incoming notes, pads, pitch bend, and CC messages into a 1024-entry power-of-two lock-free ring buffer.

