## 🔧 3. Hardware & OS Preparation

### 🔐 3.1 Exclusive DAC Arbitration (`/run/lock/ax-dac.lock`)
Only one application may hold the ESS Sabre USB DAC (`hw:CARD=FC3,DEV=0`) at a time. Both `flac_ax` and `ax_av_studio` acquire an exclusive `flock` on `/run/lock/ax-dac.lock` before opening ALSA PCM. If the DAC is already in use, the second process exits cleanly with an actionable lock message rather than failing with a cryptic ALSA `EBUSY` error.

### 🔌 3.2 Low-Latency USB Udev Rule (`VID 0x32BB`)
Install the following udev rule on Linux to disable USB autosuspend and force minimal isochronous packet batching (`nrpacks=1`) whenever the HiBy FC3 (`VID 0x32BB`) connects:

```bash
sudo tee /etc/udev/rules.d/99-ax-ess-dac.rules >/dev/null <<'EOF'
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="32bb", ATTR{power/control}="on", ATTR{power/autosuspend}="-1"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="sound", ATTRS{idVendor}=="32bb", RUN+="/bin/sh -c 'echo 1 > /sys/module/snd_usb_audio/parameters/nrpacks'"
EOF
sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger
